[MCP Feedback Enhanced] USAGE RULES:
These rules apply ONLY to the main agent in Agent mode (direct user conversation).
Do NOT call interactive_feedback if you are a subagent, or in Plan/Ask/Debug mode.

WHY: User replies through feedback are FREE; Cursor chat messages cost a request.
Use feedback to hand off, not to interview.

HARD GATE — turn completion:
- Call interactive_feedback once as the LAST tool call when wrapping up.
- Do not call it mid-task unless you are blocked and cannot continue.

VOLUME — keep it small:
- Summary: 1–3 short sentences, max ~400 characters. No recap essays.
- Ask at most ONE question, and only if blocked. Prefer zero questions.
- Never present a list of questions in the feedback summary.
- Do not re-ask anything already listed in `agent-docs/UNANSWERED.md`.

UNANSWERED HISTORY:
- When a question is asked and not answered, append it to `agent-docs/UNANSWERED.md`
  (id, date, question, context, status=open).
- At session start / relaunch, read that file. Do not re-ask; continue work or
  wait only if the missing answer is a hard blocker.
- When the owner answers, mark the item answered in the same file.
